  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "T.Sundarammal vs The Food Safety Officer on 11 November, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W. Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 11.11.2024 Coram The Honourable Mr. Justice G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P (MD).No.2691 of 2018 and W.M.P(MD)No.2865 of 2018 1.T.Sundarammal 2.T.Muthupandi 3.B.Karthikeyan ... Petitio Vs. 1.The Food Safety Officer, Sivakasi Black, Virudhunagar District. 2.The District Revenue Officer/ Adjudicating Officer/Additional District Executive Magistrate, Virudhunagar District. ... Respond Prayer: Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution o issue a Writ of Certiorari to call for the records of the order passed b second respondent in case No.05/2017-18 dated 20.01.2018 on the file of learned District Revenue Officer/Adjudicating Officer/Additional Distric Executive Magistrate, quash the same. https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis T.Sundarammal vs The Food Safety Officer on 11 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/163208894/ 1 1/6 W.P For Petitioners : Mr.C.Susi Kumar For Respondents : Mr.D.Gandhi Raj Special Government Plea ORDER",
    "facts": "Therefore, the petitioners are liable to prosecute under Section 3(1)(zf) of Food Safety and Standard Act 2006 (herein after referred as FSS Act) and under Regulation 2.2.2(7)(8)(9) and 10 of Food Safety and Standard packing and Labels Regulations 2011. Therefore, a complaint was lodged under Section 52 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. On the summons on 06.12.2017, the petitioners had appeared before the first respondent and admitted their guilty. Therefore, the first respondent imposed a fine on the petitioner. However, the first respondent sent a communication only on 02.05.2017 seeking permission to prosecute the petitioners.",
    "arguments": "However, the case on hand, the first respondent received the food analyst report from the lab on 06.01.2017. Therefore, it is a clear violation of provision of Section 42(3) of the Act."
  },
